  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A positive integer \\(N\\) with three digits in its base ten representation is chosen at random, with each three-digit number having an equal chance of being chosen. The probability that \\(\\log_2N\\) is an integer is",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(0\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\frac3{899}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{225}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{300}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\frac1{450}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "There are \\(999-100+1=900\\) three-digit integers. The three powers of \\(2\\) among them are \\(128,256,\\) and \\(512.\\) Thus the probability is \\(\\frac{3}{900}=\\frac{1}{300}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "An integral base-\\(2\\) logarithm means \\(N\\) is a power of \\(2\\)",
        "List the powers of \\(2\\) from \\(100\\) through \\(999\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
